    spec_verdict_forgeable_from_example_name_2026-08-17, 1, "2026-11-09 p3-mine2: FIXED in the live seed producer. Live path located: parse_test_output in src/compiler_rust/driver/src/cli/test_runner/execution.rs scavenged counts from any line containing both substrings example/failure. Replaced with strict tally-shape matcher parse_bdd_tally_line: only '<int> example|examples, <int> failure|failures' with optional trailing (NNms) counts; example names mentioning both words and checkmark-prefixed summary-shaped names are ignored. 4 new regression unit tests (name-with-keywords, summary-shaped name, ms-suffix, partial shapes); all 11 execution.rs parse tests PASS (cargo test -p simple-driver --lib parse_test_output). End-to-end on the fixed debug binary: the 2026-08-17 forge probe now reports Results: 1 total, 1 passed, 0 failed (was 33/1/32) and a genuinely failing spec still fails. The two pure-Simple .spl parsers were already hardened in 2026-08; the Rust seed parser was the missing piece. Deployed-seed redeploy verification pending."

